OXT-Beyond%OXT-Beyond is an open source app creation platform for Windows, macOS and Linux. It continues OpenXTalk Lite and uses the same English-like xTalk scripting language.%%It provides an easy path to coding and app creation for those starting out, learning to program, or creating their first app, and a fast route to a working app for experienced developers.%%With OXT-Beyond, you can:%- Create a user interface by drag & dropping objects onto a stack window.%- Use an English-like coding language to add logic and actions to your app.%- Include graphics, multimedia, or animation.%- Process text and data easily.%- Edit your app while it is running (no waiting for it to compile first).%- Build standalone apps for Windows and Linux, on a Mac also for macOS,%  and (with additional free software) for Android.%- Create SQL database and server applications using the same language.%%Credits%OpenXTalk Lite was started by Terry Little (TerryL) in 2023, and built and maintained by Tom Perry (tperry2x) from version 0.91 to 1.15, with contributions from Paul McClernan (OpenXTalkPaul) and other members of the OpenXTalk community. OXT-Beyond is based on OpenXTalk Lite 1.15 and on the LiveCode Community engine by LiveCode Ltd and its contributors. The OXT-Beyond icon up to 0.2.1-rc.6 was adapted from Tom Perry's OpenXTalk Lite icon. Parts of the IDE's dark mode are adapted from HyperXTalk by Emily-Elizabeth Howard, docmeth02 and its other contributors.%%OXT-Beyond project:%<ln>https://github.com/SethMorrowSoftware/OpenXTalk-Beyond%%OpenXTalk community:%<ln>https://www.openxtalk.org%%OXT-Beyond is free software, licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3.
